---
/** Arms the reveal system. Must render once, as early in <body> as possible.
 *
 *  The inline script is deliberately NOT a module: module scripts are deferred
 *  until after parsing, which would show the content, then hide it, then
 *  reveal it. This runs synchronously before first paint, so the hidden state
 *  is never visibly applied to something that was already on screen.
 *
 *  It is also the whole JS-off story: with scripting disabled this attribute
 *  never appears, `html[data-reveal-ready]` never matches, and every
 *  [data-reveal] element renders at full opacity. Nothing is stranded. */
---

<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-reveal-ready', '');
</script>
